{
  "info": {
    "name": "CELLS API",
    "description": "Import this file, then set the collection variable baseUrl (default http://localhost:8080/api/v1). Run Auth > Login first: it stores accessToken for every other request. Each request carries its cURL equivalent in its description. Local email: start Mailpit with `docker compose up -d` and read the inbox at http://localhost:8025. The 'native app' requests in Auth show how the Android/iOS app logs in (header X-Client-Type: native, refresh token in the body).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080/api/v1"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "roomId",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "devotionId",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "memberId",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "pushToken",
      "value": "example-fcm-registration-token"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "submissionId",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "reportId",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "key": "churchId",
      "value": "1"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns an access token (stored automatically) and sets the refresh cookie.\n\ncURL:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST \"{{baseUrl}}/auth/login\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n  \"email\": \"leader@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"your-password\"\n}'\n```",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"leader@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"your-password\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body && body.accessToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Current user",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The logged-in user.\n\ncURL:\n\n```\ncurl -X GET \"{{baseUrl}}/auth/me\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}\"\n```",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (native app)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Client-Type",
                "value": "native"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same as Login, but with the header X-Client-Type: native. The refresh token comes back in the response body (field refreshToken) instead of a cookie, and no cookie is set. The Android/iOS app sends this header on every request. The server honors it only when the request has no Origin header (Postman, curl) or an Origin listed in app.cors.allowed-origins (the app: https://localhost). A page of the website sending it still gets the cookie.\n\ncURL:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST \"{{baseUrl}}/auth/login\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-Client-Type: native\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n  \"email\": \"leader@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"your-password\"\n}'\n```",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"leader@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"your-password\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b && b.accessToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken); }",
                  "if (b && b.refreshToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh (native app)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Client-Type",
                "value": "native"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Native mode: send the saved refresh token in the body. Each call returns a NEW refresh token (stored automatically); the old one stops working, and reusing it logs the account out everywhere.\n\ncURL:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST \"{{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-Client-Type: native\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}'\n```",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b && b.accessToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken); }",
                  "if (b && b.refreshToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout (native app)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Client-Type",
                "value": "native"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Native mode: revokes the refresh token sent in the body. Returns 204.\n\ncURL:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST \"{{baseUrl}}/auth/logout\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-Client-Type: native\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}'\n```",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
