            "description": "Public. A leader signs up without an invitation. Creates a NEW church (never joins an existing one by name) that stays 'not verified' until an administrator verifies it, plus a LEADER account, and logs the person in. pastorName is typed text, not an account. pastorEmail is optional and only the administrator sees it. acceptRules must be true. Until verified the church is limited to 3 active rooms and 30 members. Rate-limited like login (429 when too many requests). 409 if the email already has an account. Native mode: the session comes back with refreshToken in the body.\n\ncURL:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST \"{{baseUrl}}/auth/register-leader\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-Client-Type: native\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n  \"fullName\": \"Grace Leader\",\n  \"email\": \"grace.leader@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"a-strong-password-123\",\n  \"churchName\": \"Grace Fellowship\",\n  \"pastorName\": \"Pastor Daniel Cruz\",\n  \"pastorEmail\": \"pastor@example.com\",\n  \"acceptRules\": true\n}'\n```",
            "auth": {
