            "description": "Deletes the logged-in person's own account (Google Play requirement). Log in first as the account you want to delete. Body: the current password, asked again as a safety check. Returns 204 and clears the website refresh cookie. A wrong password returns 422 (not 401). Members leave their rooms and lose their answers and EXP; a leader with active rooms gets 422 (archive them first); a pastor with assigned leaders gets 422; administrators get 422. The account is anonymised (name 'Deleted user', unusable password) and can never sign in again. DESTRUCTIVE: use a throwaway account.\n\ncURL:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST \"{{baseUrl}}/account/delete\" \\\n  -H \"Accept: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}'\n```",
